# DataGuardian Codebase Knowledge Graph & Token Optimization Rules

# Codebase Knowledge Graph (codebase-memory-mcp)

This project uses codebase-memory-mcp to maintain a knowledge graph of the codebase.
ALWAYS prefer MCP graph tools over grep/glob/file-search for code discovery to optimize token usage.

## Priority Order for Token Savings:
1. `search_graph` — Find functions, classes, routes, variables by pattern
2. `trace_path` — Trace who calls a function or what it calls
3. `get_code_snippet` — Read specific function/class source code
4. `query_graph` — Run Cypher queries for complex patterns
5. `get_architecture` — High-level project summary

## DataGuardian MCP Native Tools (backend/datahub/mcp_client.py)
- `mcp_get_lineage(urn)` — Traverses 10+ node graph downstream
- `mcp_get_schema(urn)` — Retrieves entity schema & SQL definition
- `mcp_apply_quarantine_tag(urn, reason)` — Tags damaged entities as QUARANTINED
- `mcp_update_deprecation(urn, note)` — Sets deprecation aspect
- `mcp_patch_sql(urn, new_sql)` — Restores HEALTHY status
